      "anchor": "lifts-odd-fixed-weight-closure",
      "title": "Why the common jumps survive weighted trace approximation",
      "hypotheses": "Global semisimplicity and the translated trace estimates give a lattice tower. The bounded-weight period comparison supplies compatible crystalline frames and the stated uniform operator estimates. Each auxiliary member has the same labelled jumps.",
